# Copy to .env.local and fill in your own project's values.
#
# Find them in the Supabase dashboard: Project Settings → API
#   VITE_SUPABASE_URL      — the Project URL
#   VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY — the "anon public" key (newer projects call this the
#                            "publishable" key, sb_publishable_...). Never the
#                            service_role / secret key: it bypasses row-level
#                            security entirely.
#
# Both values here are safe to ship in the frontend bundle — the anon key is
# designed to be public, and the database is locked down by the row-level
# security policies in supabase/schema.sql.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL="https://your-project-ref.supabase.co"
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY="sb_publishable_your_key_here"
